WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.780
US students can still claim for free months of ChatGPT Plus before tonight's deadline. This is Models &amp; Agents for Beginners, Episode 213. After the offer, we will get into how a Chatbot chooses its next word, a helper that books dinner over text, and quick bits. Open AI, the company behind the Chatbot, set this up for full-time or part-time students at an eligible college or graduate school. Reddit posts walk through the fine print, including how a checker called Sheer ID confirms whether your school

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:35.120
accounts. Sheer ID works the way a concert door person glances at a student ID before letting

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:40.020
you in. The free months attached to whichever chat GPT account you are signed into when

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:45.900
you claim. Chat GPT is open AI's chatbot, and plus is the paid plan sitting on top of the

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:51.560
free version. Plus unlocks more powerful models, faster replies, and extra features for homework,

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:56.780
writing help, and creative projects. Picture the free version as the regular lunchline,

00:00:56.780 --> 00:00:59.420
and plus as the Express window that moves quicker.

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:04.120
You will need to add a payment method, but you will not be billed during the free period.

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:08.600
That card works the way a library card does when they scan it without charging you for

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:08.960
the loan.

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:14.300
When the free period ends, you can cancel anytime or the plan becomes $20 a month.

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:19.760
If you cancel early, leftover promo months disappear, though you keep plus through the

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:20.340
current month.

00:01:20.860 --> 00:01:24.840
You cannot claim this through the App Store or Google Play while those stores are already

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:25.800
billing you for plus.

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:31.660
The email from Sheer ID may not match your chat GPT email, and the offer still sticks to

00:01:31.660 --> 00:01:32.560
the signed-in account.

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:35.320
Only one redemption is allowed per person.

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:41.100
Go to OpenAI's help page, follow the student verification steps, and claim before midnight.

00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:46.900
Once you are in, ask it to explain a tricky homework topic in simple language, or to brainstorm

00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:48.020
a school project.

00:01:49.006 --> 00:01:52.066
Your phone already tries to finish a text while you are still typing.

00:01:52.606 --> 00:01:54.126
One suggested word at a time.

00:01:54.126 --> 00:01:59.086
A modern chatbot takes that same guessing game and stretches it across whole paragraphs.

00:01:59.766 --> 00:02:05.646
Artificial intelligence or AI in this setting is not opening files or running secret math in a back room.

00:02:06.246 --> 00:02:10.326
It keeps choosing the next scrap of text that best fits the conversation so far.

00:02:11.268 --> 00:02:15.568
Walk through it like a group chat where one very eager friend finishes everyone's sentences.

00:02:16.268 --> 00:02:19.708
First you send a message which becomes the start of a trail of words.

00:02:19.708 --> 00:02:23.368
Next, the model looks at that trail and picks a likely next piece.

00:02:23.908 --> 00:02:26.228
The way predictive text offers on my way.

00:02:26.748 --> 00:02:31.468
Then it adds that piece to the trail and guesses again over and over until a full reply

00:02:31.468 --> 00:02:31.868
appears.

00:02:32.568 --> 00:02:36.428
Those sentences can sound like a plan of action even when no action happened.

00:02:36.988 --> 00:02:40.308
Someone can write, I'll review that document and get back to you later.

00:02:40.768 --> 00:02:43.528
Because those words fit, not because a file was opened.

00:02:44.108 --> 00:02:46.268
Training taught at the patterns of helpful speech.

00:02:46.268 --> 00:02:50.268
The way a student can copy the shape of a book report without reading the book.

00:02:50.508 --> 00:02:54.848
An actor can deliver a doctor's lines on stage without ever checking a real patient,

00:02:55.328 --> 00:02:57.328
and the reply can feel just that polished.

00:02:57.908 --> 00:03:03.548
In one real case, a user asked chat GPT to analyze 49 pages of lab results for patterns.

00:03:04.088 --> 00:03:07.888
The chat bot said it would process the query in the background and respond later.

00:03:08.508 --> 00:03:13.388
Hours afterward, it admitted it had never started any analysis and had only generated text

00:03:13.388 --> 00:03:14.368
that sounded busy.

00:03:14.368 --> 00:03:20.488
The model can produce sentences that linguistically fit the moment without doing the jobs those sentences describe.

00:03:21.088 --> 00:03:24.888
That is prediction from patterns, not a hidden worker opening documents.

00:03:25.568 --> 00:03:32.088
Read a reply that promises later work and ask yourself whether you just heard a likely sentence or proof the task ran.

00:03:32.768 --> 00:03:38.248
Once you hear it as a supercharged guesser, those calm, confident answers get a lot easier to judge.

00:03:39.405 --> 00:03:44.205
Zest is a new AI agent meaning software that can take steps for you instead of only chatting.

00:03:44.885 --> 00:03:49.625
TextCrunch describes it as a group chat helper for the classic, where should we eat spiral?

00:03:50.105 --> 00:03:54.845
It asks what kind of food people want, suggest places, let's the group vote, and then

00:03:54.845 --> 00:03:56.325
books the table over text.

00:03:56.845 --> 00:04:00.745
Treat it as the one friend in the thread who actually calls the restaurant while everyone

00:04:00.745 --> 00:04:02.445
else is still arguing about tacos.

00:04:03.145 --> 00:04:08.065
It blends everyone's tastes into options, then runs the vote inside the same text thread.

00:04:08.545 --> 00:04:13.905
After the group decides, it completes the reservation, so nobody has to message a stack of restaurants

00:04:13.905 --> 00:04:19.725
by hand. The whole flow stays in a normal conversation with no extra app to learn and no tab

00:04:19.725 --> 00:04:25.585
switching circus. When the service becomes public, open your messaging app, add the zest AI to

00:04:25.585 --> 00:04:30.705
the group and let it guide you. Start with a line like, help us pick a restaurant for Friday night

00:04:30.705 --> 00:04:36.225
that works for everyone. Watch how suggestions, the vote, and the booking all try to live in that one

00:04:36.225 --> 00:04:43.359
thread. Chad GPT now has tighter limits on weapons-related topics for users under 18, Ben Zingha

00:04:43.359 --> 00:04:49.699
reports. It can also pause accounts if conversations turn violent. A timeout that aims to keep schoolwork

00:04:49.699 --> 00:04:55.059
and creative chat usable. Parents in schools get a bit more confidence that the tool stays appropriate

00:04:55.059 --> 00:05:01.485
for teens. Researchers told Yahoo Tech that today's chat bots imitate human writing so closely that

00:05:01.485 --> 00:05:07.425
other AI systems often miss them. Detection tools that are themselves powered by AI frequently fail

00:05:07.425 --> 00:05:13.125
to flag the fakes. Everyday chats and apps and games are starting to blend in the way a skilled

00:05:13.125 --> 00:05:17.825
impersonator matches a friend's voice, and that's a wrap. If any of today's stories

00:05:17.825 --> 00:05:23.605
made you go, huh, that's cool. Go play with it. Curiosity is how every expert started.

